# Security

When code touches user input, auth, API routes, or sensitive data:

- Apply engineering foundations first (always-applied rule).
- Prefer the project's security skill; if none, load this plugin's `skills/ankyr-security/SKILL.md` if installed. Security floors always apply.
- Load its `references/` only when the skill directs.

Key rules: no injection (parameterize), no XSS (escape/sanitize), CSRF protection on state changes, server-side validation with allow-lists, no client-exposed secrets, no credential/PII logging, generic user-facing errors.
